  m_Name: Q06_Junction_Asymmetry
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::PNJunctionLab.AssessmentQuestion
  questionId: q06_asym_w
  topic: 2
  topicTag: 3. P-N Junction Equilibrium
  shortSummaryLabel: Asymmetric Depletion W
  promptText: In a Silicon P-N junction with lightly doped P side (NA = 1e15 cm^-3) and heavily doped N side (ND = 1e17 cm^-3), how does depletion width W divide?
  options:
  - Depletion extends 100x farther into the lightly doped P side (xp = 100 * xn)
  - Both sides always share identical depletion penetration (xp = xn = W / 2)
  - Depletion extends 100x farther into the heavily doped N side (xn = 100 * xp)
  - Built-in potential V0 drops to 0 V whenever NA != ND
  correctIndex: 0
  explanation: 'Charge balance NA * xp = ND * xn forces the depletion region farther into the lighter-doped side: xp = W * ND / (NA + ND).'
  recommendedStation: Station 4
